## Jelee ignore rules (G01.4).
##
## Eight groups in the order of docs/requirements-source.md G01.4. Every
## pattern has its own comment line directly above it; tools/gitignore-check
## enforces that, enforces that each pattern appears in docs/toolchain.md
## ("被忽略的产物"), and runs ignored/not-ignored probes against every rule
## (tools/gitignore-check/probes.txt). Adding a pattern therefore means adding
## a comment, a probe and the docs/toolchain.md entry in the same commit.
## Lines starting with "##" are section headings, "#" lines explain the next
## pattern. Git does not support trailing comments.

## 1. Build outputs and dependencies

# make build / scripts/make.ps1 build: bin/jelee, bin/jelee-cli, bin/jelee-migrate.
bin/
# Vite build output (web/dist) and scripts/release.py archives (dist/release).
dist/
# npm workspace dependencies (repository root and web/).
node_modules/
# Go build cache when GOCACHE is pointed inside the checkout; bootstrap keeps it in .tools/cache.
/.gocache/
# Go test binaries from `go test -c`.
*.test
# Delve debug binaries written next to the package (__debug_bin1234).
__debug_bin*
# Native executables and libraries built by hand; release archives carry them, Git never does.
*.exe
# Windows dynamic libraries (cgo or hand builds).
*.dll
# Linux shared objects.
*.so
# macOS dynamic libraries.
*.dylib
# Vite dependency pre-bundling cache.
.vite/
# TypeScript incremental build state (tsc -b).
*.tsbuildinfo
# ESLint --cache state.
.eslintcache
# Python bytecode cache directories of scripts/*.py.
__pycache__/
# Stray Python bytecode files (scripts run with -B, but direct imports may still write them).
*.py[cod]

## 2. Toolchain and local installs (G51)

# Pinned tool installs; no trailing slash because worktrees may link .tools to a shared directory.
.tools
# Generated wrappers and links into .tools (.bin/go, .bin/npm, .bin/golangci-lint).
.bin/
# Python virtual environments.
.venv/
# Generic tool caches (go-build, npm, pip) when redirected into the checkout.
.cache/
# Vendor archives downloaded by bootstrap scripts before verification.
tools/vendor-downloads/

## 3. Tests: coverage, reports, browser output and generated fixtures

# Go coverage profiles and reports (coverage.out, coverage.html).
coverage.*
# Go profiles and other test outputs (cpu.out, mem.out, c.out).
*.out
# Generic report directories (lint, bench, acceptance).
reports/
# Playwright and other test runners' result directories.
test-results/
# Playwright HTML report when written outside .testdata.
playwright-report/
# Playwright blob reports (sharded runs).
blob-report/
# Python coverage data.
.coverage
# Generated media fixtures (make fixtures).
.testfixtures/
# Local test state: databases URLs, reports, soak logs, agent env files.
.testdata/
# Throwaway test databases (*.test.db) are covered by *.db in group 6.

## 4. Runtime data and logs

# Runtime data root and every derived folder below it (transcodes, subtitles, mediainfo, images, index).
/data/
# Log files written by local runs.
*.log
# Log directory of local runs.
/logs/

## 5. Environment and secrets

# Local environment file.
.env
# Environment variants (.env.local, .env.production).
.env.*
# The documented example stays tracked.
!.env.example
# PEM certificates and private keys.
*.pem
# Private keys.
*.key
# PKCS#12 key stores.
*.p12
# PKCS#12 key stores (Windows extension).
*.pfx
# Java key stores.
*.jks
# Generic credential files (OAuth clients, cloud SDKs).
credentials.json
# Cloud service account keys.
service-account*.json
# netrc credentials.
.netrc

## 6. Databases

# SQLite files and their journals (*.sqlite, *.sqlite3, *.sqlite-wal).
*.sqlite*
# Other local database files: *.test.db, copies of a legacy jellyfin.db for legacy-import.
*.db
# SQLite write-ahead log of a *.db file.
*.db-wal
# SQLite shared-memory index of a *.db file.
*.db-shm
# SQLite rollback journal of a *.db file.
*.db-journal
# pg_dump custom-format dumps.
*.dump
# Compressed SQL dumps.
*.sql.gz
# Local PostgreSQL data volume (bind mount of docker compose).
/postgres-data/
# Alternative local PostgreSQL data directory name.
/pgdata/

## 7. IDE and operating system files

# JetBrains (GoLand, WebStorm, Rider) project state.
.idea/
# VS Code local state; shared configuration is re-included below.
.vscode/*
# Shared extension recommendations stay tracked.
!.vscode/extensions.json
# Visual Studio local state.
.vs/
# Vim swap files.
*.swp
# Vim swap files (second generation).
*.swo
# Editor backup files.
*~
# Windows thumbnail cache.
Thumbs.db
# Windows thumbnail cache (older name).
ehthumbs.db
# Windows folder settings.
[Dd]esktop.ini
# Windows recycle bin on shares.
$RECYCLE.BIN/
# macOS Finder metadata.
.DS_Store
# KDE Dolphin folder settings.
.directory
# Microsoft Office lock files.
~$*

## 8. Temporary files

# Temporary files (listed before .tmp/ so the directory rule decides for it).
*.tmp
# Scratch directory of tools and agents.
.tmp/
# Scratch directory.
tmp/
# Backup copies.
*.bak
# Local NFO write-back backups (G39 keeps NFO backups outside Git).
*.nfo.jelee.bak*
# Merge leftovers.
*.orig
# Rejected patch hunks.
*.rej
